    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 183\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5485-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the public health law and the social services law,\n      in relation to automatic enrollment and recertification  simplifi-\n      cation for Medicaid eligible recipients\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill would require Medicaid coverage to be automatically renewed\nfor certain individuals, prior to a definitive determination  that  such\nindividuals  continue  to  be Medicaid eligible, unless there has been a\nfinding of lack of  eligibility  for  Medicaid.  This  bill  effectively\ncreates  a  presumption  that  an  individual continues to be in need of\nMedicaid services unless the state shows it is not the case.\n\n  While I appreciate  the  intent  of  simplifying  Medicaid  enrollment\nprocedures,  as drafted this bill raises serious concerns. By seeking to\nauthorize  Medicaid  services  without  a  check  for  eligibility,  the\nproposed  language  runs contrary to federal law that requires the state\nto demonstrate financial eligibility  prior  to  obtaining  or  renewing\nMedicaid  coverage, and could jeopardize federal financial participation\nin the program. Medicaid expenditures for long-term care are  increasing\nat  a significant rate and are substantially impacting the state budget.\nExtension of Medicaid eligibility to individuals  who  have  yet  to  be\ndetermined eligible would result in unbudgeted costs.\n \n  This  bill  would  also  require significant systems work, which would\nfurther drive costs to  the  state,  disrupt  efforts  to  update  aging\nsystems  infrastructure,  and delay the consolidation of Medicaid eligi-\nbility requirements for all Medicaid cases within NY  State  of  Health.\nFor these reasons, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
